Enter Tiger Cloud (formerly Timescale), built directly on open-source PostgreSQL. Tiger Cloud introduces three fundamental capabilities to standard Postgres: First: Hypertables. To standard SQL queries, a hypertable looks like a normal PostgreSQL table. Under the hood, TimescaleDB automatically partitions the table across time and space into discrete chunks. This eliminates the notorious B-Tree write slowdown of traditional databases, allowing Tiger Cloud to ingest over three trillion metrics per day without performance degradation! Second: Hyp

